# COMPONENT

## KnowledgeWorkbench

### STYLE

full-fledged-with-standalone

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.knowledgeworkbench

### DESCRIPTION

Forms Information Candidates for human work. The current starter supports
Candidate registration and search using a stable standalone user identity and
the CNCF-managed native persistent application datastore. Proposal formation,
review and approval belong to subsequent Phase 1 work.

### COMPONENTLET

#### public-candidate

#### candidate-admin

# COMPONENTLET

## public-candidate

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for public Candidate registration and search.
The current factory constructs only the primary participant; this declaration
does not enable MCP publication.

# COMPONENTLET

## candidate-admin

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for administrative Candidate work. The current
factory does not instantiate this participant or publish its services through MCP.

# SERVICE

## Candidate

### DESCRIPTION

Registers and searches starter Information Candidates for the current user.
Operations require a stable user identity and the native persistent application
datastore supplied by the CNCF Subsystem.

### OPERATION

#### registerCandidate

##### DESCRIPTION

Creates a native InformationCandidate using a required name and optional
description. This command persists a new entity and returns its native id and name.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidate

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidateResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

#### listCandidates

##### DESCRIPTION

Returns accessible InformationCandidates as items. Optional text matches a
case-insensitive substring of name or description; without text, all accessible
rows are eligible. Optional offset and limit apply through native query paging.
This query does not create candidates.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidates

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidatesResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

# ENTITY

## InformationCandidate

### Attribute

| name        | type     | multiplicity |
|-------------+----------+--------------|
| id          | entityid | 1            |
| name        | name     | 1            |
| description | InformationCandidateDescription | ?            |

# VALUE

## RegisterCandidate

- input-kind :: COMMAND

### Attribute

| name        | type   | multiplicity |
|-------------+--------+--------------|
| name        | name   | 1            |
| description | InformationCandidateDescription | ?            |

## ListCandidates

- input-kind :: QUERY

### Attribute

| name   | type   | multiplicity |
|--------+--------+--------------|
| text   | InformationCandidateSearchText | ?            |
| offset | int    | ?            |
| limit  | int    | ?            |

## InformationCandidateDescription

### Attribute

| name  | type   | multiplicity |
|-------+--------+--------------|
| value | string | 1            |

## InformationCandidateSearchText

### Attribute

| name  | type   | multiplicity |
|-------+--------+--------------|
| value | string | 1            |

## RegisterCandidateResult

### Attribute

| name | type     | multiplicity |
|------+----------+--------------|
| id   | entityid | 1            |
| name | name     | 1            |

## ListCandidatesResult

### Attribute

| name  | type                   | multiplicity |
|-------+------------------------+--------------|
| items | InformationCandidate | *            |
